  "worked_solution": "We find the constants $A$ and $B$ using the initial conditions. \n\n- Substituting $y(0)=8$ into the general solution gives\n\n$$\nA=8.\n$$\n\n- To apply the condition ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=0,$ we first differentiate $y$ to get\n\n$$\n{y}^{\u2032}=-A{e}^{-x}+B{e}^{-x}-Bx{e}^{-x}.\n$$\n\nSubstituting ${y}^{\u2032}(0)=0$ into the above gives\n\n$$\n-A+B=0.\n$$\n\nUsing the fact that $A=8$ gives $B=8.$\n\nTherefore, the solution to the initial value problem is\n\n$$\ny=8{e}^{-x}+8x{e}^{-x}.\n$$",
